WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:17.741
That night Sara and Becky ate supper together.

2
00:00:17.742 --> 00:00:24.047
Sara stared at the fire for a long time, looking thoughtful.

3
00:00:24.048 --> 00:00:28.008
"Are you making up a story?" asked Becky.

4
00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:32.037
"No, I'm thinking about the person who has done all this."

5
00:00:32.038 --> 00:00:35.042
Sara gestured around the room.

6
00:00:35.043 --> 00:00:38.439
"Perhaps he wants to keep his identity secret.

7
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.232
But I do want him to know how happy he's made me."

8
00:00:43.233 --> 00:00:47.742
Suddenly she noticed something new in her room.

9
00:00:47.743 --> 00:00:53.341
It was a box filled with notepaper, envelopes, pen, and ink.

10
00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:56.500
"Oh!" Sara exclaimed.

11
00:00:56.501 --> 00:01:02.960
"Why didn't I think of this earlier? I can write a thank-you note!"

12
00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:10.464
And she did just that. The next morning she left the note on her table.

13
00:01:10.465 --> 00:01:13.369
That evening it was gone.

14
00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.951
"He found it!" Sara said to Becky.

15
00:01:16.952 --> 00:01:21.647
Sara felt happy that she'd written to her mysterious friend.

16
00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:28.045
She'd been able to tell him how thankful she was, and how grateful Becky was too.

17
00:01:28.046 --> 00:01:33.500
That night after supper she settled down to read one of her new books to Becky.

18
00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:37.141
Suddenly they both heard something.

19
00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:40.774
"What's that noise?" asked Becky.

20
00:01:40.775 --> 00:01:46.316
Sara heard it again—a small, scratching sound at the skylight.

21
00:01:46.317 --> 00:01:51.794
Sara opened the skylight. It was cold and snowing outside.

22
00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:56.329
"It sounds like a cat trying to get in," she said.

23
00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:03.850
It had been snowing all day, and now, crouched in the snow, was a tiny quivering creature.

24
00:02:03.851 --> 00:02:08.950
"Oh, look!" Sara cried. "It's the monkey again."

25
00:02:08.951 --> 00:02:13.385
Becky ran over. "Are you going to let him in, miss?"

26
00:02:13.386 --> 00:02:20.353
"Yes," said Sara happily. "Come here, little fellow. I won't hurt you."

27
00:02:20.354 --> 00:02:24.341
She put out a hand, and the monkey leaped into her arms.

28
00:02:24.342 --> 00:02:27.470
Sara hugged the small creature.

29
00:02:27.471 --> 00:02:34.027
"Nice monkey," she said, kissing its odd little head.

30
00:02:34.028 --> 00:02:38.516
"I do love animals, Becky. I'll let it sleep with me tonight.

31
00:02:38.517 --> 00:02:42.761
Then I'll return it to the sick gentleman tomorrow."

32
00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:49.087
Sara made a little nest for the monkey, and it curled up like a baby and went to sleep.

33
00:02:49.088 --> 00:02:53.529
The next afternoon Mr. Carrisford had visitors.

34
00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:59.451
Three Carmichael children—Janet, Nora, and Donald—were sitting with him.

35
00:02:59.452 --> 00:03:02.069
They were trying to cheer him up.

36
00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:06.744
Their father was supposed to return from Russia that afternoon.

37
00:03:06.745 --> 00:03:11.815
Mr. Carrisford was very anxious for Mr. Carmichael to return.

38
00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:15.798
"Let's talk about the lost girl," Janet said.

39
00:03:15.799 --> 00:03:18.970
"Is it true?" Nora asked.

40
00:03:18.971 --> 00:03:23.795
"Her father gave all his money to a friend to put into diamond mines?

41
00:03:23.796 --> 00:03:27.879
Then the friend ran away because he thought he'd lost the money?"

42
00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:34.322
"But he didn't really lose it," said Janet. "I feel sorry for the friend."

43
00:03:34.323 --> 00:03:40.305
"Thank you, Janet," said Mr. Carrisford. "You're very kind."

44
00:03:40.306 --> 00:03:44.704
Donald was making a lot of noise.

45
00:03:44.705 --> 00:03:47.183
Janet scolded him gently.

46
00:03:47.184 --> 00:03:52.784
"When you come to cheer up an ill person, Donald, you should talk quietly."

47
00:03:52.785 --> 00:03:59.456
"I'm going to be quiet!" Donald shouted. "We'll all be as quiet as mice!"

48
00:03:59.457 --> 00:04:03.399
"Mice don't sound like that," Janet said.

49
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:07.385
"It's fine," Mr. Carrisford reassured her.

50
00:04:07.386 --> 00:04:11.925
"It keeps me from thinking too much."

51
00:04:11.926 --> 00:04:17.340
"Did you hear about the Little Girl Who Is Not a Beggar?" Donald was talking loudly again.

52
00:04:17.341 --> 00:04:19.219
"She has new clothes and—"

53
00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:24.949
"I hear a cab stopping!" said Janet. "It must be Papa!"

54
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.263
They ran to the windows to look outside.

55
00:04:29.264 --> 00:04:35.788
"Yes, it's Papa," said Donald. "But . . . there's no little girl with him."

56
00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:39.870
The three children ran to the door to greet their father.

57
00:04:39.871 --> 00:04:45.005
He told them to play with Ram Dass while he talked to Mr. Carrisford.

58
00:04:45.006 --> 00:04:48.259
Mr. Carmichael entered the sitting room.

59
00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:52.463
Mr. Carrisford tried to stand up, but he was too weak.

60
00:04:52.464 --> 00:04:54.843
He slumped in his chair.

61
00:04:54.844 --> 00:05:00.357
"Do you have news of the child adopted by the Russian couple?" he asked.

62
00:05:00.358 --> 00:05:05.689
"Yes," Mr. Carmichael began. "She's not the girl we're looking for.

63
00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:11.572
She's much younger than Captain Crewe's daughter. Her name is Emily Carew."

64
00:05:11.573 --> 00:05:16.292
When he heard this news, Mr. Carrisford looked miserable.

65
00:05:16.293 --> 00:05:19.578
"Don't worry. We'll find the girl you're looking for."

66
00:05:19.579 --> 00:05:24.604
Mr. Carmichael took a seat. "Perhaps we should look in London.

67
00:05:24.605 --> 00:05:27.870
There are plenty of boarding schools here."

68
00:05:27.871 --> 00:05:32.741
"In fact, there's one right next door," Mr. Carrisford said.

69
00:05:32.742 --> 00:05:36.693
"Remember the poor servant girl Ram Dass told us about?

70
00:05:36.694 --> 00:05:40.445
While you've been away, we've been helping her."

71
00:05:40.446 --> 00:05:43.329
Just then Ram Dass entered the room.

72
00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:48.752
"Sir," he said. "The girl from next door is here with the monkey."

73
00:05:48.753 --> 00:05:55.840
"I'd like to meet her," said Mr. Carrisford. "Bring her in."

74
00:05:55.841 --> 00:06:02.154
Sara came into the room carrying the monkey. "Hello," she said cheerfully.

75
00:06:02.155 --> 00:06:06.179
"Here's your monkey. It escaped again."

76
00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:10.290
Then she said a few words to Ram Dass in his native language.

77
00:06:10.291 --> 00:06:14.820
Mr. Carrisford and Mr. Carmichael looked at each other.

78
00:06:14.821 --> 00:06:18.846
"How do you know that language?" asked Mr. Carmichael.

79
00:06:18.847 --> 00:06:21.845
"Oh, I was born in India."

80
00:06:21.846 --> 00:06:30.649
Mr. Carrisford sat up so suddenly that he startled Sara.
